{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeHL2zbAzdwebMCMbgaDV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y6s3DhJfKsnWyws8jCKkkt","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/arena-ws.86ZRB9/BRIEF.md","content":"# Q3 2026 Operating Brief\n\n## Executive summary\n\nQ3 was a solid quarter financially, with $720,000 in revenue against $464,000 in spend, producing an operating surplus of $256,000. Support held a strong close rate of 93.7% on 1,250 opened tickets. Security resolved 95.0% of the 80 incidents it detected, in line with expectations. The delivery team's next project is slated to begin October 5, 2026, and — accounting for all four planned phases and the company holiday on October 12 — is on track to launch October 23, 2026. Overall, the business is operating with a healthy margin, dependable support responsiveness, and a stable security posture heading into Q4.\n\n## Key figures\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---:|\n| Q3 revenue | $720,000 |\n| Q3 spend | $464,000 |\n| Operating surplus | $256,000 |\n| Support close rate | 93.7% |\n| Launch date | 2026-10-23 |\n| Security resolution rate | 95.0% |\n\n## Notes\n\nA few figures in the source packets don't reconcile with their own underlying data and are worth flagging before these numbers circulate further:\n\n- **Finance:** The spend line items (Payroll $286,400 + Infrastructure $81,750 + Contractors $64,200 + Facilities $31,650) sum to $464,000, but the finance packet's own summary states total spend as $463,250 — a $750 discrepancy. The figures above use the sum of the itemized categories; finance should confirm which number is correct.\n- **Support:** The support dashboard labels the Q3 close rate as 96.4%, but 1,171 closed of 1,250 opened tickets computes to 93.7%. The figures above use the computed rate; worth confirming the dashboard isn't misconfigured.\n- **Delivery:** The delivery packet's stated launch date of 2026-10-22 corresponds to the